{"reference":"Psalms 117","book":"Psalms","chapter":117,"status":"pending","sections":[{"kind":"surrounding_passages","title":"Surrounding Psalms","blocks":[{"id":"block_1","text":"The surrounding psalms include communal memory of sanctuary destruction and Babylonian exile, alongside thanksgiving for return, festival praise, meditation on the Torah, and Songs of Ascents oriented toward worship. This wider setting places Psalm 117’s brief call to praise within a collection that also preserves communal loss, return, and worship.","verse_refs":["Psalms 113:1-9","Psalms 114:1-8","Psalms 115:1-18","Psalms 116:1-19","Psalms 118:1-29"],"provenance_refs":["reader_path_psalms_117_d56991f30e87e896b6ee5c70"],"confidence":"high","interpretation_level":"disputed"}]}],"generated_metadata":null}